w maybe not the most  effective especially if you're like us a  startup who's like exploring the  solution space and trying to improve so  that's that's basically my two main  recommendations get a get a glue person  on your team who knows a little bit of  both worlds and then used in the  Shepherd your data science algorithms  into your product and do it in the same  repository it'll be fine  Thanks  [Applause]  so the question is how easy is it to  define the glue person and it's not  extremely easy not as easy as finding a  software person but I would say like  we've hired a lot of data scientists  over the years and we've hired to glue  people I was the first one at my company  and then we hired another one and it's  doable it's about the same frequency  that you'd find a good data scientist  with I think dependent but the key is  like really write your job spec well  know what you're looking for don't  expect someone that's going to come in  and come up with your new deep learning  algorithm and do good software you just  need someone who you know has enough of  a math background and during your  interview you know that your data  scientist can talk to them decide it to  your question yeah interesting paths  didn't know what I wanted to do when I  grew up so I just did computer science  did some software engineering for a  couple of years I didn't want to do  something more interesting so I did a  master's and computer vision and I  actually ended up working in software  again but this time on implementing  software algorithms much in that kind of  translation type mode of operation and  then I found software I'd then I found  first few software and they were really  looking for someone to kind of fill that  niche and luckily they hired me  so with that I'd like to thank all three  of our speakers again both Ryan EULA and  Donna let's give them another round of  applause  [Applause]
 

